V3DRender 0.06: kit 5, compute on every QPU
============================================

Mesa's programs (riscos-mesa's V3DTri) draw a few tiles on the Pi 4 and
then stop, with pixels waiting for the GPU's processors (QPUs) to run
their fragment shaders. Mesa's lists and shaders look right. Kit 4's
compute job ran on one QPU only. Kit 5 adds test 8: compute jobs of 64,
then 4096 workgroups, each of which writes its own number, so that
threads run on every QPU. If some QPUs never finish a thread, test 8
stops the same way Mesa's frames do, and the numbers that didn't arrive
show which work went missing.

The V3DRender module is 0.06, as you have loaded.

Before you start
- A Pi 4, Pi 400 or CM4 with RISC OS 5.30 or later. V3DDriver not
  loaded. Copy this folder to a hard disc.

The test
1. Double-click Check. It loads V3DRender 0.04 (replacing 0.02 or 0.03
   if loaded) and RISC3D 0.03, then runs V3DCheck and V3DJob. Tests 1-7
   passed before; 8 is new. Both programs write to Results, and
   *V3DRender's figures are added at the end.
2. Optional: double-click HangTest again (as in kit 2).
3. Send Results back.

The compute job is the first program to run on the GPU's own processors
under V3DRender. If one of the new tests freezes the machine, restart
and say which number it had reached.
